1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,012
How Antibiotic Resistance Threatens Modern Medicine.

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:10,825
Antibiotic resistance represents one of the most urgent threats to global public health in the 21st century.

3
00:00:10,825 --> 00:00:29,262
The 2024 GRAM Project study published in The Lancet projects that more than 39 million people could die directly from antibiotic-resistant infections between 2025 and 2050, with annual deaths reaching 1.91 million by 2050 — a nearly 70 percent increase from 2021.

4
00:00:29,262 --> 00:00:41,600
The CDC's 2021–2022 Antibiotic Resistance Threats Report confirmed that the COVID-19 pandemic reversed prior progress against antimicrobial resistance in the United States.

5
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:47,100
Hospital-acquired resistant infections rose sharply, erasing years of gains.

6
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:57,012
In a Lancet commentary published in September 2024, CDC leaders warned that antimicrobial resistance threatens to reverse a century of medical progress.

7
00:00:57,012 --> 00:01:07,025
Routine procedures — including joint replacements, cesarean sections, and cancer chemotherapy — depend on effective antibiotics to prevent infection.

8
00:01:07,025 --> 00:01:17,562
The World Health Organization has identified a critical pipeline problem: too few new antibiotics are in development, particularly against dangerous Gram-negative bacteria.

9
00:01:17,562 --> 00:01:24,950
Meanwhile, misuse of antibiotics in human medicine and agriculture accelerates the emergence of resistant strains.

10
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:33,937
The GRAM Project estimates that antimicrobial resistance currently kills at least 1.27 million people annually, more than HIV or malaria.

11
00:01:33,937 --> 00:01:38,775
Deaths among adults aged 70 and older have risen by more than 80 percent.

12
00:01:38,775 --> 00:01:50,587
Without coordinated global action — including investment in new antibiotics, improved surveillance, and antibiotic stewardship — the foundation of modern medicine faces an uncertain future.

